      tour: `Chapter 18 is the reckoning. Mrs. Carmichael takes Sara into her arms and explains everything: Carrisford is Captain Crewe's old friend; the mines came in spectacularly; Carrisford has spent two years searching for Sara, who turns out to have been next door. Miss Minchin, facing Carrisford's solicitor, is informed that her treatment of Sara constitutes something the law takes an interest in. She proposes to act now as if she had known who Sara was all along. The solicitor declines to accept this framing. Sara, asked how she has been treated, gives an answer that is not a lie but is also not a recitation of grievances. She says: I tried not to be miserable.`,
